From ef5f1bb145d74fc888d11a31d2c5978c08804146 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Auchter <michael.auchter@ni.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Sep 2019 16:46:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 068/110] nvmem: Add NI TLV NVMEM support and fix MAC address
 provisioning
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a new nitlv_nvmem driver that interprets the tag-length-value (TLV)
format used on the X410. The driver acts as an nvmem proxy: it consumes
an nvmem cell providing raw access to the TLV EEPROM and exports named
cells (keyed by tag) for use by client drivers.

Fix the at24 EEPROM driver to expose device tree cell definitions to the
NVMEM framework by enabling add_legacy_fixed_of_cells during probe. Without
this, consumers calling devm_nvmem_cell_get() received -ENOENT and failed
to probe, breaking the dependency chain:

  EEPROM (at24) → TLV parser (nitlv_nvmem) → Ethernet (gem3)

Also enable add_legacy_fixed_of_cells in nitlv_nvmem so its own child
nodes are registered as NVMEM cells.

Reorder MAC address lookup priority in of_get_mac_address() to check
NVMEM cells before the local-mac-address property. The latter may be
set by firmware to a random value when no valid MAC is found in hardware,
while NVMEM cells are explicitly configured in device tree and should
take precedence.

Add probe diagnostics to nitlv_nvmem to aid diagnosis of cell lookup
failures and TLV data validation errors. These logs should be converted
to dev_dbg() once the driver is considered stable.

Signed-off-by: Michael Auchter <michael.auchter@ni.com>
Signed-off-by: Bjoern Bachmann <bjoern.bachmann@emerson.com>
---
